# Writeout

!!_T#Documents# ++PR1:Writeout++ is the word processor of the suite. It has real pages, a Navigation pane, a status bar and a ribbon that works like Microsoft Word, and everything you write is Keydown text!

[Open Writeout](/writeout) · [Phone version](/writeout/mobile/new/)


::divider{wavy|Writeout|blue}
## The ribbon

| Tab | What you will find |
| --- | --- |
| ++B;}Home++ | Clipboard, Font, Paragraph, Styles (including Keydown Styles), Editing and Margin Marks |
| @dymo-2@Insert@ | New Page, Table, Picture, Link, Header & Footer, Symbols, Captions, Cards & Blocks, Badges, Templates, Equation, and Bulleted and Numbered Lists |
| ++GL/}Layout++ | Margins, Orientation, Size, Pages View, Print Preview, Color Preview, Page Number Format, Watermark, Page Border and Line Spacing |
| !!=GL#References# | Table of Contents, Footnotes, Cross-references, Citations, Sources, Bibliography and Mail Merge |
| ++B1:Review++ | Word Count, Find & Replace, Comments, Track Changes, Read Aloud, Un-format and Re-format, the Annotator, Ink Drawing, Readability, Word Goal, Version History and Protect Document |
| ++PR.:View++ | View, Visual and Source modes, Pages, Continuous and Focus views, Zoom, and the Layout switch |
| ++TU4)Help++ | Help Deck, Keydown Guide and Shortcuts |

## Three ways to edit

The ++G@)View++ tab has three modes, and you can switch any time without losing anything:

* @softinset-5@View@ shows the finished page. Click to edit, and Keydown tags turn into formatting as you type them!
* ++PR^]Visual++ is the same page with the formatting controls visible, like a classic word processor!
* =C=Source=C= shows the raw Keydown text, with colors for tags, headings, chips and code. Press ++O[]Tab++ to insert an indent (a leading `|`)!

## Writing with Keydown

Type a tag and press ++GL/}Space++, and it becomes formatting. Press ++TU""Enter++ at the end of a line to format every tag still on that line. For example:

```
# A heading
This is **bold**, this is *italic*, and this is `code`.
++R+A glossy red chip++
::note Remember this
```

Use **Un-format** to turn a whole page back into tags, and ++G+)Re-format++ to format everything again. Tags that could not be formatted are underlined so mistakes are easy to find. The full language is in the [Keydown guide](#/keydown-start)!

## Pages

* ++G=New Page++ (Insert tab, or Ctrl/Cmd+Enter) adds a real page break, written as `::pagebreak`. The ++TU4)Pages++ list in the side pane shows every page!
* ++L&&Print Preview++ shows the true page size and margins, and !!0GL#Color Preview# shows grayscale or color-blind views!
* ++TU3]Margins, Orientation and Size++ are in Layout, and are saved in the file's header!

## Saving and exporting

Documents are saved as `.kd` files. **File > Home** lists every saved document so you can rename or switch between them, and **Share > Keep a file on this computer** keeps a real file updated as you type (Chrome, Edge and Opera). Export gives PDF, Word, OpenDocument, plain text and EPUB. See [Files](#/files) for the rest!

## Collaboration and history

* Review > Comments and @receipt-4@Track Changes@ work like other word processors!
* @longshadow-3@Version History@ (and **Save Version**) lets you look at and restore earlier copies!
* Share & Chat edits the same document live with other people. See [Sharing](#/sharing)!

## Inserts worth knowing

* Cards & Blocks adds document blocks like a table of contents, a cover page, callouts, columns, tabs, checklists and footnotes lists. See [Document blocks](#/keydown-blocks)!
* @origami-5@Badge@ opens a picker for small labeled chips!
* ++T0:Equation++ inserts math in LaTeX, drawn by KaTeX!
* ++C!!Templates++ starts from a ready-made layout!
* ++PR3(3D scenes++ and Inkpath drawings can be embedded, and fonts like Kubasta and Monogram are bundled!
